ed_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly why only `interprocess_lock` is used, unlike the cited cache.py exemplar's two-tier `threading.Lock`+`interprocess_lock` — i.e. that flock on distinct open file descriptions already serializes the same-process worker-thread case the fix targets.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.369,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'using the pattern src/rebar/_snapshot/cache.py already runs for snapshot materialization (cache.py:215-228)'","cache.py:215-216 comment: 'Single-flight: in-process per-SHA lock, then cross-process flock' — the cited pattern is two-tier (threading.Lock at :217 then interprocess_lock at :221)","Plan's concurrency model is same-process: 'serves concurrent handlers on a worker thread'; the AC-3 test (test_similar_tickets_index.py:382) spawns two threading.Thread in one process","interprocess_lock (git_fetch.py:62-77) uses fcntl.flock on a per-open-file-description fd, which does serialize same-process threads — so a single lock is defensible, but the divergence is unexplained"],"finding":"The plan cites cache.py:215-228 as the pattern it reuses, but that exemplar layers an in-process `threading.Lock` (`_sha_lock`, cache.py:217) BEFORE `interprocess_lock` (cache.py:221); the plan adopts only `interprocess_lock` and never states why the in-process tier is omitted, even though its harm model and new test run two threads in a single MCP worker process.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f90b3687cda81cc75","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"The fix: single-flight recovery on the existing interprocess lock","norm_id":"nb389bbe9358ab218","priority":0.231,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two MCP request handlers on the worker thread enter recovery concurrently within one process","A reviewer or implementer wonders whether flock-only serializes same-process threads and whether the dropped in-process lock was an oversight"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to the fix section noting that the in-process `_sha_lock` tier of the cache.py pattern is deliberately omitted because `interprocess_lock`'s flock serializes same-process threads (each caller opens its own fd / open file description), so a single cross-process lock covers both the multi-process and the same-worker-thread cases the plan names.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the exact lock-file path/name derived from the index path (e.g. `index.sqlite.rebuild.lock`) so all cross-process recovery callers acquire the identical lock.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.435,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'acquires interprocess_lock ... on a lock file beside the index'","Portability fallback is atomic-mkdir, which requires an agreed-upon path across callers"],"finding":"The lock-file identity is under-specified: 'a lock file beside the index' does not name the exact filename or confirm all recovery callers across processes derive the identical path, which is load-bearing for interprocess_lock to actually serialize them.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbc88b07dc704b43f","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"The fix section","norm_id":"ne7d96d31216af159","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two executors compute different lock-file paths (e.g. relative vs absolute, or per-connection temp) and never actually mutually exclude"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State the concrete lock path, e.g. `path + \".rebuild.lock\"`, in the fix section and the first acceptance criterion.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether catchup.py write path also acquires the recovery interprocess_lock (or why the sqlite write lock + the recovery flock cannot race), closing the gap between the two lock domains.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'catchup.py:196 opens its transaction with BEGIN IMMEDIATE on a connection whose PRAGMA busy_timeout'","'take the lock, then re-check before acting' — the lock only covers recovery callers","The 'what this does not fix' paragraph scopes the residual window to a caller that opened BEFORE a peer entered recovery, but does not address a caller that opens and begins writing DURING a peer's recovery via the sqlite-only path"],"finding":"The plan serializes recovery callers against each other via a new interprocess_lock, but catchup.py writers serialize only on sqlite's own write lock and are not stated to take the recovery lock. A fresh catchup that opens successfully and runs BEGIN IMMEDIATE can still run concurrently with a recovery-branch discard, reproducing harm #2 (committing into an inode a concurrent unlink detaches).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0c03dc2af245e3b6","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"The fix section / 'What this does not fix'","norm_id":"nb4f02dfc8688a76c","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor A enters recovery and acquires the flock; Executor B's connection opens successfully (post-rebuild-start or on a different connection) and runs BEGIN IMMEDIATE without ever taking the flock, so A's discard/rebuild races B's write"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"f554c722dd96f393","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["7910ae97d389c583",5893],"description_boxes":["8b6fa01313ce51af",0],"file_impact":["b32962939ec087c7",2],"ticket_id":["78388b4224abbe4a",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":278974,"cache_write_tokens":88216,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":3611.6,"input_tokens":388928,"llm_calls":29,"llm_ms":121230.0,"output_tokens":19278,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":131840.5,"verify_requests":7},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_struc